{"uncertainty": 0.3, "outcome": "Delivered a self-checking SystemVerilog testbench, tick_timer_cov_tb.sv, that extends the approved idle testbench, and a coverage report that names the points this testbench cannot reach. It has not been simulated or measured. The platform's coverage.read run will decide whether it passes and meets the coverage targets.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "coverage_report", "title": "tick_timer coverage plan and expected-unreachable points", "summary": "This report covers the approved RTL [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.design-under-test.a1] and serves [requirement:req-33bb46282b]. The new testbench drives a stimulus for each line and branch of the design. (1) Reset, applied at the start and again at the end. (2) A one-shot count from 3 that expires, stops EN and raises irq with IE set. (3) A STATUS write with bit 0 clear, which leaves EXPIRED set, then a write-one-to-clear. (4) A periodic count from 2 that reloads on each expiry. (5) An expiry and a clear at the same edge, where the expiry should win. (6) A CTRL write while running at count zero, which should suppress the expiry, and a CTRL write while EN is already 1, which should not reload. (7) Stopping with CTRL=0, after which the count should hold. (8) Reads of all four addresses, including the default STATUS arm. For toggle coverage, wdata is driven to 32'hFFFFFFFF and back to 0, LOAD to 16'hFFFF and back to 0, and the count runs down the full 65535 steps from 16'hFFFF to 0, so every count bit should toggle both ways. Two sets of design signals cannot toggle with W=16. rdata[31:16] is always 0 by construction, and unused_wdata is a constant &{1'b0,...} = 0. These points are expected to remain unhit and are justified as unreachable for this parameterisation, not excluded. No coverage numbers are reported here. They come only from the platform's coverage.read run over this testbench. The approved idle testbench [artifact:prj-4fd2403e98.testbench.a1] passed 5 checks in [run:run-0001], but that run